# MadGraph5 batch script: lt~ lt > qt qt~ NP<=1 NPGG<=1
# in vibegraph_toy_UFO, restricted by restrict_tensor.dat.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   The tensor-tensor four-fermion contact in both of its spellings at once --
#   Sigma(-1,-2,2,1)*Sigma(-1,-2,4,3) under NP, and the same operator written as
#   the gamma-gamma chains FeynRules would have produced under NPGG -- beside the
#   s-channel vector exchange they both interfere with. Three diagrams, so the
#   contact's sign and normalisation are measurable per helicity, and the two
#   spellings can be compared against each other diagram by diagram in MadGraph's
#   own AMP() before anything on this side evaluates either.
#
# The model path is repo-relative to the vendored UFO; build.sh rewrites it to
# the work-area copy it stages under output/models/. This model is ours, so its
# restrict cards live inside the model directory and are staged with it.
#
# `display interactions` prints the count MadGraph's own interaction splitting
# arrives at (one interaction per coupling-order tuple, import_ufo.add_interaction)
# into the build log, which is where extract_interactions.py reads it from.
#
# The order bound is explicit on every row of this model: an unbounded generate
# runs MadGraph's WEIGHTED search, which would drop the higher-order diagrams the
# interference needs.
import model validation/ufo/vibegraph_toy_UFO-tensor
display interactions
generate lt~ lt > qt qt~ NP<=1 NPGG<=1
output ll_to_qqx_toy_tensor -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 250
set ebeam2 250
set use_syst False
done
